Z||000000||87PegasusGT||06-07-2000||01:28 PM||||I have Fiero shop's Blue bulbs and one of them only works on brights? Replace the bulb? Will any blue Halogen work?<BR>Also: My door ajar light keeps coming on while I am driving!!!!! What the H@#? !!!???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fret Naught||06-07-2000||03:07 PM||||I don't know about the headlight, situation, but the door ajar light is most likely a bad ground or real dirty switch in one of your doors. clean them real good, and make sure they are mounted firmly. See if that works.<P>How about this, I was just told that when I leave work at night, when I shift gears, my back up lights come on??? any thoughts on that one?||||reg||7
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||06-07-2000||03:20 PM||||Thanks for the tip. It just started doing it. I'll see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000003||dman||06-07-2000||07:37 PM||||Hi Fred, on some cars the backup light switch is mounted onto the shifter. Chances are good that your car is like this. If you take the center console apart you can get to the shifter. The switch is plainly visible. Perhaps some crud fell in there. You wouldn't believe all of the coins, matchbooks, etc that can accumulate in that area. While you are at it, you may wish to check and possibly re-adjust your shift/select cables.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fret Naught||06-07-2000||07:48 PM||||Thanks Dman, I will check it out this weekend||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||06-07-2000||07:52 PM||||Hey, I couldn't help but notice you live in the Northwest.  When I lived in Silverdale, WA, and it rained or misted 99% of the time, my hood ajar switch would short out and stay that way until the rain stopped for more than a few days.  In other words, the door ajar light never cleared until I disconnected the hood switch.  Here in GA, we're in a drought, so no problem now.||||reg||6
